# Coding Guidelines
- Do not include emoji in code comments, variable names, or output
- Write production-quality code with clear naming conventions and consistent style
- Avoid unnecessary comments or clutter
- Maintain consistent indentation and spacing
- Use blank lines to separate logical code blocks
- Preferably, Keep each file around 200–250 lines for readability and maintainability
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Follow language-specific best practices and standard conventions
